export const notesHtml = "<!doctype html><html lang=\"en\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width,initial-scale=1\">\n<title>Colosseum 1.1.9 — Release notes</title>\n<style>body{margin:0;background:#101114;color:#e7e5de;font:18px/1.7 system-ui,sans-serif}main{max-width:780px;margin:auto;padding:48px 24px 96px}a{color:#f3ce4b}nav{font-size:15px;margin-bottom:48px}h1{font-size:clamp(32px,6vw,52px);line-height:1.15}h2{font-size:25px;margin-top:48px;color:#f3ce4b}li{padding:5px 0}code{overflow-wrap:anywhere;font-size:.9em}</style>\n</head><body><main><nav><a href=\"/\">Colosseum</a> / Release notes</nav><article><h1>Colosseum 1.1.9</h1>\n<p>Windows release published 19 October 2026. This release starts at <code>v1.1.8</code> and includes the catalogue delivery migration, Universes, shared reliability improvements, the first-party updater migration, and the Linux candidate fixes. Feria and Vinyl source is integrated behind Coming Soon; neither world is available in 1.1.9. There is one standard edition, with optional accounts and local use.</p>\n<h2>Online catalogues and content API</h2>\n<ul><li>Native manga/anime, Comics and Theatre catalogue reads use the content API and prepared query assets, avoiding whole-catalogue database downloads on those paths.</li><li>Prepared landings, progressive shelves, smaller fact shards and deferred decoding reduce the work needed before useful catalogue content appears.</li><li>Manga volume counts and BookWalker-sourced cover URLs travel through the catalogue service. Existing media-cover providers remain in use.</li><li>Universe definitions and owned artwork use published online content, allowing compatible content updates without rebuilding the app.</li><li>One Piece tribute artwork is fetched online and cached. Native add-on artwork and the existing 55-extension logo table remain bundled.</li><li>Production content publication and Windows installer checks passed. Loading speed is not universally matched; remaining Comics speed/alignment work is deferred.</li></ul>\n<h2>Universes</h2>\n<ul><li>Universes is the fourth world, with franchise banners, category filters, keyboard navigation, and a separate Tributes carousel.</li><li>Structured cross-media shelves cover James Bond, Marvel, Star Trek, Star Wars, DCAU, Avatar, Studio Ghibli, Shonen Jump, One Piece, Dragon Ball, Naruto, and Attack on Titan.</li><li>One Piece includes the East Blue, Paradise, New World, and Final Sea atlases, interactive island markers, arc previews, sea navigation, and online artwork. Its standard Universe page carries the 56-work catalogue.</li><li>Improved poster preloading, focus handling, artwork identities, and map placement.</li><li>Shared TopBar navigation adapts to narrow windows and includes the Universes pill.</li></ul>\n<h2>Vault and Extensions</h2>\n<ul><li>Desktop Vault has a native media-library layout with browsing rails, poster cards, folder breadcrumbs, detail sheets, and the shared Colosseum theme.</li><li>Extensions opens the native House page with rotating franchise wallpapers, a glass tray, and extension tiles. Chain, House, and Store navigation is connected. House banners use installed extension artwork with bundled offline fallbacks.</li></ul>\n<h2>Reading and reliability</h2>\n<ul><li>Continue reopens standalone local comics in the correct reader and assigns their identity before restoring saved reading progress.</li><li>Fixed PDF text search and navigation in Reader2.</li><li>Improved Theatre replay, audiobook final-chapter completion, progress flushing during profile departure/shutdown, and local-file identity across restarts.</li><li>Improved account refresh recovery after timeouts and restarts, disabled avatar storage handling, unavailable trackers, shutdown ordering, and Windows helper cleanup.</li><li>Linux fixes cover X11 sizing, WSLg placeholder screens, unavailable tracker guards, Reader2 test linkage, and the Watch Party shutdown crash. Portable packaging includes AppRun and dependency checks. Linux 1.1.9 distribution materials are being finalized; the Linux installer is not included in this Windows publication.</li></ul>\n<h2>Coming Soon and platform scope</h2>\n<ul><li>Feria and Vinyl remain blocked through normal and indirect world entry. Ordinary release builds ignore the Vinyl development environment opt-in.</li><li>Feria services remain lazy while the world is disabled. Full browser and music feature qualification is deferred.</li><li>Feria and Vault are permanently outside Android&#x27;s scope. Android packaging excludes their desktop dependencies and desktop Vinyl QML.</li></ul>\n<h2>Updates</h2>\n<ul><li>Windows update discovery moves to <code>https://getcolosseum.world/updates/stable.json</code>, using the existing production signing trust and retaining signed legacy compatibility.</li><li>Windows users on 1.1.8 need one manual installation of 1.1.9 to migrate. Later Windows releases can use the first-party feed. Linux remains manual-update-only.</li><li>The Windows installer is accompanied by its canonical update manifest, production Ed25519 signature and SHA-256 checksums.</li></ul>\n<p>Windows fresh installation, manual 1.1.8 migration, representative local library/progress/ preference preservation, and the real NSIS restart/healthy-boot component passed. The complete native automatic signed discovery/download/shutdown/install/restart chain remains unqualified; manual installation is the supported 1.1.8 migration route.</p>\n<h2>Known issues</h2>\n<ul><li>Comics loading speed and row alignment still need improvement; this work is deferred to 2.0.0.</li><li>Navigating the One Piece tribute can unexpectedly expose Vault. This reported issue is deferred to 2.0.0.</li></ul>\n<h2>Testing and maintenance</h2>\n<ul><li>Expanded automated coverage for Universes, One Piece, Vault, account refresh, standalone comic Continue, PDF search, and release publishing.</li><li>Improved QtWebEngine codec CI configuration and compiler caching.</li><li>The source history includes Chocolatey metadata for the 1.1.8 Windows package. This does not publish a 1.1.9 Chocolatey package.</li><li>Development guidance and canonical event-memory integration were updated.</li><li>AniList, CloudStream, Aniyomi, and Nuvio integration feasibility was researched; these integrations are not shipped features of this release.</li></ul></article></main></body></html>\n";
